  - id: letter_to_laodicea
    displayName: The Knock at Laodicea's Door
    flavorText: Christ rebukes lukewarm Laodicea for its false sense of riches and
      stands knocking at the door, calling it to repent and dine with him.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: The most sharply rebuked of the seven - 'lukewarm' Laodicea is warned
      it will be 'spued' out of Christ's mouth, called wretched, miserable, poor,
      blind, and naked despite thinking itself rich; counseled to buy true riches
      from Christ, with the image of Christ standing at the door and knocking, and
      the promise of a shared throne to whoever opens.
    deliveredByManagerId: jesus_revelation
    managerId: letter_to_laodicea
